---
title: Cilantro Peanut Noodles
description: Soba noodles tossed with seared mushrooms and cabbage in a savory-spicy peanut sauce, finished with fresh cilantro and scallion.
course: main
cuisine: Asian
servings: 2
time required: 15 minutes
prep time: 5 minutes
cook time: 10 minutes
source: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7Yo54RiBUx0&ab_channel=ProHomeCooks
image: https://jessicainthekitchen.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/Peanut-Ginger-Noodle-Salad9707.jpg
tags:
  - noodles
  - peanut
  - vegetarian
  - quick
  - lunch
---

In a #bowl{} combine the @peanut butter{3%tbsp}, @sambal{3%tbsp}, @soy sauce{3%tbsp}, @honey{1%tbsp}, @sesame oil{1%tbsp}, juice of @lime{1}, @garlic{1%clove}(grated), @ginger{1%small knob}(grated), and @water{1/4%cup}. Whisk into a smooth sauce and set aside.

Heat a drizzle of @oil{} in a #skillet{} over medium heat. Tear up the @mushrooms{1%cup} and add them to the pan, tossing to coat, and let them cook until browned.

Slice the @cabbage{1/2%cup} leaves and add to the mushrooms. Season with @salt{}, adding more oil if needed, and cook another ~{1-2%minutes} before removing to cool.

Meanwhile, boil the @soba noodles{2%servings} in a #pot{} according to package instructions, then drain.

In the cleaned skillet, add the peanut sauce and let it bubble on low heat to thicken.

Once thickened, toss in the cooked noodles, mushrooms, and cabbage until everything is coated. Top with @scallion{}(chopped) and @cilantro{}(chopped) and serve.
